{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C7pSwJteapYRjzoKCE4EDt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Generic slotmap-style arena.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! A storage container that hands out [`Token`]s as opaque handles\n4\t//! to its values.  Tokens carry a generation counter so that\n5\t//! reusing a slot after removal invalidates any outstanding tokens\n6\t//! — the safe equivalent of the C `*mut T` use-after-free.\n7\t//!\n8\t//! Every Phase-4 collection that needs \"address an object by\n9\t//! handle, not by raw pointer\" sits on top of this — most notably\n10\t//! the `Quic` connection arena, which holds every live connection\n11\t//! and lets the secondary indexes (`connection_by_id`, `connection_by_net`, …)\n12\t//! store `ConnectionToken`s as their values.\n13\t\n14\tuse core::marker::PhantomData;\n15\t\n16\tuse crate::Error;\n17\t\n18\t/// Opaque handle into an [`Arena<T>`].  `Copy`, 64 bits total.\n19\t///\n20\t/// The `T` parameter is purely a phantom — it stops you from using\n21\t/// a `Token<Connection>` to index into an `Arena<Stream>`.  The\n22\t/// runtime check still lives in the generation counter inside the\n23\t/// arena.\n24\t#[derive(Debug)]\n25\tpub struct Token<T> {\n26\t    idx: u32,\n27\t    generation: u32,\n28\t    _phantom: PhantomData<fn() -> T>,\n29\t}\n30\t\n31\t// Manual PartialEq/Eq/Hash so that `Token<T>` works even when `T` is not\n32\t// `PartialEq`.  Two tokens are equal when their physical slot index and\n33\t// generation counter match — the `T` phantom plays no role at runtime.\n34\timpl<T> PartialEq for Token<T> {\n35\t    fn eq(&self, other: &Self) -> bool {\n36\t        self.idx == other.idx && self.generation == other.generation\n37\t    }\n38\t}\n39\t\n40\timpl<T> Eq for Token<T> {}\n41\t\n42\timpl<T> core::hash::Hash for Token<T> {\n43\t    fn hash<H: core::hash::Hasher>(&self, state: &mut H) {\n44\t        self.idx.hash(state);\n45\t        self.generation.hash(state);\n46\t    }\n47\t}\n48\t\n49\t// `Copy` and `Clone` written by hand so they don't depend on `T:\n50\t// Copy`.  Tokens are always `Copy` regardless of what `T` is.\n51\timpl<T> Copy for Token<T> {}\n52\timpl<T> Clone for Token<T> {\n53\t    fn clone(&self) -> Self {\n54\t        *self\n55\t    }\n56\t}\n57\t\n58\timpl<T> Token<T> {\n59\t    /// Construct a synthetic token with explicit `idx` and `generation` fields.\n60\t    /// This is `pub(crate)` — external code must go through [`Arena::insert`].\n61\t    /// Used internally when code must name an arena slot from data that already\n62\t    /// carries the slot index and generation.\n63\t    pub(crate) fn synthetic(idx: u32, generation: u32) -> Self {\n64\t        Self {\n65\t            idx,\n66\t            generation,\n67\t            _phantom: PhantomData,\n68\t        }\n69\t    }\n70\t}\n71\t\n72\t/// A slot in the arena storage vector.\n73\tenum Slot<T> {\n74\t    Free {\n75\t        next_free: Option<u32>,\n76\t        generation: u32,\n77\t    },\n78\t    Filled {\n79\t        generation: u32,\n80\t        value: T,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc65f024-1847-48ea-8039-b3ad326afc33","uuid":"f5123223-524e-432a-abdb-2ebc016e20a0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T08:29:23.442Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/arena.rs","content":"//! Generic slotmap-style arena.\n//!\n//! A storage container that hands out [`Token`]s as opaque handles\n//! to its values.  Tokens carry a generation counter so that\n//! reusing a slot after removal invalidates any outstanding tokens\n//! — the safe equivalent of the C `*mut T` use-after-free.\n//!\n//! Every Phase-4 collection that needs \"address an object by\n//! handle, not by raw pointer\" sits on top of this — most notably\n//! the `Quic` connection arena, which holds every live connection\n//! and lets the secondary indexes (`connection_by_id`, `connection_by_net`, …)\n//! store `ConnectionToken`s as their values.\n\nuse core::marker::PhantomData;\n\nuse crate::Error;\n\n/// Opaque handle into an [`Arena<T>`].  `Copy`, 64 bits total.\n///\n/// The `T` parameter is purely a phantom — it stops you from using\n/// a `Token<Connection>` to index into an `Arena<Stream>`.  The\n/// runtime check still lives in the generation counter inside the\n/// arena.\n#[derive(Debug)]\npub struct Token<T> {\n    idx: u32,\n    generation: u32,\n    _phantom: PhantomData<fn() -> T>,\n}\n\n// Manual PartialEq/Eq/Hash so that `Token<T>` works even when `T` is not\n// `PartialEq`.  Two tokens are equal when their physical slot index and\n// generation counter match — the `T` phantom plays no role at runtime.\nimpl<T> PartialEq for Token<T> {\n    fn eq(&self, other: &Self) -> bool {\n        self.idx == other.idx && self.generation == other.generation\n    }\n}\n\nimpl<T> Eq for Token<T> {}\n\nimpl<T> core::hash::Hash for Token<T> {\n    fn hash<H: core::hash::Hasher>(&self, state: &mut H) {\n        self.idx.hash(state);\n        self.generation.hash(state);\n    }\n}\n\n// `Copy` and `Clone` written by hand so they don't depend on `T:\n// Copy`.  Tokens are always `Copy` regardless of what `T` is.\nimpl<T> Copy for Token<T> {}\nimpl<T> Clone for Token<T> {\n    fn clone(&self) -> Self {\n        *self\n    }\n}\n\nimpl<T> Token<T> {\n    /// Construct a synthetic token with explicit `idx` and `generation` fields.\n    /// This is `pub(crate)` — external code must go through [`Arena::insert`].\n    /// Used internally when code must name an arena slot from data that already\n    /// carries the slot index and generation.\n    pub(crate) fn synthetic(idx: u32, generation: u32) -> Self {\n        Self {\n            idx,\n            generation,\n            _phantom: PhantomData,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// A slot in the arena storage vector.\nenum Slot<T> {\n    Free {\n        next_free: Option<u32>,\n        generation: u32,\n    },\n    Filled {\n        generation: u32,\n        value: T,","numLines"