n_token)\n1936\t    }\n1937\t\n1938\t    /// Convenience wrapper around [`Self::create_connection`] for the\n1939\t    /// client side; `addr` is required.\n1940\t    pub fn create_client_connection(\n1941\t        &mut self,\n1942\t        addr: &SocketAddr,\n1943\t        start_time: Instant,\n1944\t        preferred_version: u32,\n1945\t        sni: Option<&str>,\n1946\t        alpn: Option<&str>,\n1947\t        _callback: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n1948\t    ) -> Option<&mut Connection> {\n1949\t        // C: picoquic_create_client_cnx — wraps picoquic_create_cnx with\n1950\t        // null CIDs, then runs picoquic_start_client_cnx and rolls back\n1951\t        // on failure.  Callback installation is folded in here; the Rust\n1952\t        // shape stores the boxed callback on Connection, which is the\n1953\t        // moral equivalent of `cnx->callback_fn`/`cnx->callback_ctx`.\n1954\t        self.create_connection(\n1955\t            ConnectionId::with_size(0)?,\n1956\t            ConnectionId::with_size(0)?,\n1957\t            Some(addr),\n1958\t            start_time,\n1959\t            preferred_version,\n1960\t            sni,\n1961\t            alpn,\n1962\t            true,\n1963\t        )\n1964\t    }\n1965\t\n1966\t    /// Default callback enablement for path-state events on new\n1967\t    /// connections.\n1968\t    pub fn set_path_callbacks_default(&mut self, are_enabled: bool) {\n1969\t        self.are_path_callbacks_enabled = are_enabled;\n1970\t    }\n1971\t\n1972\t    /// Default thresholds for the path-quality-update callback.\n1973\t    pub fn set_default_quality_update(&mut self, pacing_rate_delta: u64, rtt_delta: Duration) {\n1974\t        self.pacing_rate_update_delta = pacing_rate_delta;\n1975\t        self.rtt_update_delta = rtt_delta;\n1976\t    }\n1977\t}\n1978\t\n1979\timpl Connection {\n1980\t    /// Begin the client-side handshake on this connection.\n1981\t    pub fn start_client(&mut self) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1982\t 